ents ${A}_{1},{A}_{2},{A}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space. Compute $P({A}_{3}|B)$ given the following probabilities:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(B|{A}_{1})=0.5, &  \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{2})=0.6, & P({A}_{2})=0.2 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{3})=0.1, & P({A}_{3})=0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186167159 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186167160 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\