iven by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186241124 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186241143 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186241144 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186241145 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186241159 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=2 \\\\ 2y+z &=0 \\\\ -x+2y+z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186241160 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=0 \\\\ -3x-y+5z &=0 \\\\ -2x-4y+z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186243890 "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-z &=16 \\\\ 15-8x &=-4y \\\\ -y+20x &=3z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186243984 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $y$ is a vector such that $x+y=0$, then $y=-x.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186243985 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $y$ and $z$ are vectors such that $x+y=z+x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $y=z.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186243994 "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{1} &=3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186244037 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186244038 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186244039 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$