\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A+20I$ and $A-15I$ on the nonzero vectors $v,w,x$ and $y$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186244292 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\overset{A+4I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A+4I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+4I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }z\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A+4I$ and $A+3I$ on the nonzero vectors $u,v,w,x,$ $y$ and $z$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [#edb/ref 17592186247003 "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{t}^{2}{y}^{′}=t+1\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247004 "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-3t{y}^{′}+{t}^{2}y=6\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247005 "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,y=2t\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247007 "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{y}^{″}-6t{y}^{′}-9y=t\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247009 "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{y}^{′}-10y=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247010 "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{e}^{t}{y}^{′}+4ty=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247014 "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+3{t}^{1/2}{y}^{″}-7y=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247015 "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+{e}^{t}{y}^{″}-{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}y=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186247017 "The secon