\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=8x(t)-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives an equation of the line in the phase space that contains all equilibrium points of the system above?"] [#edb/ref 17592186308509 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives an equation of the line in the phase space that contains all equilibrium points of the system above?"] [#edb/ref 17592186308510 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-6x(t)+8y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives an equation of the line in the phase space that contains all equilibrium points of the system above?"] [#edb/ref 17592186308513 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=6x+2y+z,\\, && y(1)=-1 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=2x-y+z,\\, && z(1)=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy$ and $Δz$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(2)≈$\n{{field-3}}\nand $z(2)≈$\n{{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186308514 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=3x+2y+z,\\, && y(0)=3 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=2x-y+3z,\\, && z(0)=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy$ and $Δz$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=2?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(2)≈$\n{{field-3}}\nand $z(2)≈$\n{{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186308515 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }3]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186308516 "Suppose we wish to approximate the solution to an initial value problem using the following numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =(xy+{y}^{2})\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)=3{x}^{2}+5x,$ find an expression for the local truncation error for the step from $x$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186308517 "Suppose we wish to approximate the solution to an initial value problem using the following numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+1,$ find an expression for the local truncation error for the step from $x$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186308518 "Suppose we wish to approximate the solution to an initial value problem using the following numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =({x}^{2}+\\sqrt{y})\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+4x+5,$ find an expression for the local truncation error for the step from $x$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186308524 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=\\frac{x+2y-z}{(x-z)^{2}},\\,