st upper bound we can form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & \\le {{field-7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|f(x)|\\le 4|x|$ whenever $|x|<1.$ Thus, taking \n\n$$\n{{field-8}},\\,{{field-9}}\n$$\n\n satisfies the definition, and we conclude that $f(x)=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186308571 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSuppose we wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={e}^{x},$ compute the local truncation error ${τ}_{21}$ for the step starting at $x=1$ with step size $Δx=0.05.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${τ}_{21}≈$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186308573 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+1,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSuppose we wish to approximate the solution using the following numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}(x+{y}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+x,$ compute the local truncation error, ${τ}_{6},$ for the step starting at $x=1$ with step size $Δx=0.2.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${τ}_{6}≈$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186308593 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)-7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t)+4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =4\\pm 7\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186308594 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =-1\\pm 