e linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186344950 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+4z &=1 \\\\ -x-2y-4z &=-1 \\\\ 3x+6y+12z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186344951 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=3 \\\\ x+2y-2z &=0 \\\\ -2x+2y-2z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186344952 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+5z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+10y &=-4 \\\\ x-5y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186344953 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-12y+12z &=-4 \\\\ 5x+16y-9z &=4 \\\\ 2x+6y-6z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186344956 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+3z &=0 \\\\ x+3y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186344957 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=-1 \\\\ x-2y &=1 \\\\ -x-5y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186344961 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 2x+(k+1)y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186344968 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $x$ is a vector such that $-x+w=w$ for some $w\\in V$, then $x=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axioms  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186344969 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ 3x+2ky &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186344971 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y &=-8 \\\\ x+ky &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186345023 "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+10.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186345024 "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, 