e blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357672 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357676 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357677 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186360532 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186360768 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2z-x &=1 \\\\ 6y+3x-2z &=2 \\\\ x+3z-y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & b & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362293 "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(-3,-1,-2)=1, &  & {f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2)=4, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2)=-3, &  & {f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ estimate the value of $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362294 "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(3,0,4)=25, &  & {f}_{x}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, &  & {f}_{z}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4),$ estimate the value of $f(3.01,0.1,3.99).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362295 "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,2,-3)=-6, & \\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=yz,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=xz,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,-3),$ estimate the value of $f(1.01,1.95,-3.02).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362352 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨0,{e}^{t},1⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨0,1,-{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186362365 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186362368 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=1,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩, \\\\ N(1) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186362381 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}⟨2{e}^{2t},1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector."] [#edb/ref 17592186362398 "Find the limit at $x=-1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<-1 \\\\ -2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=-1 \\\\ x+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362399 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le -1 \\\\ x+c\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=1.$ What is the value of the constant $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362400 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x & \\text{ for }\\,x<-2 \\\\ x & \\text{ for }\\,x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362401 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\text{ for }\\,x<-1 \\\\ 3 & \\text{ for }\\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362661 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }z\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A+I$ and $A-2I$ on the nonzero vectors $u,v,w,x,$ $y$ and $z$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186363087 "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-15{x}_{3} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186363094 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-3y+6z &=9 \\\\ -x+4z &=4 \\\\ x+y-2z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186363101 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-5y-3z &=6 \\\\ -x+2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186363108 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=2 \\\\ -2x+7y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186363217 "$$\n\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{Q}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}^{R}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} &=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2} &=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3} &=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{3}+2{q}_{1}-{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{23}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186363405 "![](images/8f/8f955ee719a4e69f0d09c678f0a74023f137efd7b5ae36d49b98706156384173.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0<x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [#edb/ref 17592186363479 "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-y+z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+z=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ &=\\lambda ⟨0,\\,,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186363486 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-yz$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+z=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,-y⟩ &=\\lambda ⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\,⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,0,\\,\\,⟩ \\\\ y+{z}^{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186363493 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y-{x}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨\\,,\\,{x}^{2},\\,2z⟩ &=\\lambda ⟨\\,,\\,1,\\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,,\\,2z⟩ \\\\ y-{x}^{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186363988 "If the following system of differential equations is written in the form ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then what is the matrix $A?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+8{x}_{1}(t) &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364027 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) &=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+t\\,{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |  |  |"] [#edb/ref 17592186364171 "$$\n\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{Q}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}^{R}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $‖{v}_{1}‖=3,$ $‖{v}_{2}‖=4,$ $‖{v}_{3}‖=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} &={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2} &={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3} &={a}_{3}-5{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364178 "$$\n\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}^{Q}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}^{R}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} &=\\frac{1}{6}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2} &=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+8{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3} &=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{3}-3{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364358 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+2y-z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186364365 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=8 \\\\ x+y &=-2 \\\\ x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186364372 "Let $R=[-2,1]\\times [-4,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x-y+4.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by