us at $t=1?$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2},\\,|t-1|⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨8{t}^{2}-2,\\,{2}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨5t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186370058 "Which of the following vector functions are continuous on $[1,4]?$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{s}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡s}\\,j+(s+1)\\,k \\\\ q(s) & =s{e}^{s}\\,i+{s}^{2}{e}^{s}\\,j-\\frac{s}{{e}^{s}}\\,k \\\\ r(s) & =\\sqrt{s}\\,i+(2-{s}^{2})\\,j+s\\operatorname{ln}⁡s\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186370065 "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186370100 "Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}$ given $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nLet $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ={{field-1}}\\,{|}_{0}^{t}=A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}=L\\{A(t)\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={A}^{′}(t)\\text{ }dt \\\\ dv={{field-3}} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ {{field-5}}, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-6}}\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186370156 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=-5x+xy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=4y-0.5xy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above for the functions $x(t)$ and $y(t).$ Select the correct options in the following statement.$\\,$\nTerm ${y}^{′}$ in the second equation represents the \n{{field-1}} \nof the \n{{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186370163 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=3x-1.5xy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=-2y+xy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above for the functions $x(t)$ and $y(t).$ Select the correct options in the following statement.$\\,$\nTerm ${x}^{′}$ in the first equation represents the \n{{field-1}} \nof the \n{{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186370170 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=2.5x-0.5xy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=-4y+0.8xy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above for the functions $x(t)$ and $y(t).$ Select the correct options in the following statement.\n\n$\\,$\nTerm ${x}^{′}$ in the first equation represents the \n{{field-1}} \nof the \n{{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186370181 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=6x-5xy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=-7y+3xy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Find the nonzero equilibrium of the model.\n\n$(${{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186370186 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} &=-2x+3xy \\\\ {y}^{′} &=7y-5xy\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey. Fin