obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =9({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }9((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ 4x(x+3){y}^{′} & =12\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[4(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}+12(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}]{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -6y & =-6{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*"] [#edb/ref 17592186379425 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=x(y-z),\\, && y(0)=-1 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=y(z-x),\\, && z(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(1)$ and $z(1).$\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(1)≈$\n{{field-2}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186379430 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &={x}^{2}+3y-z,\\, && y(0)=0 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=x+{y}^{2},\\, && z(0)=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(2)$ and $z(2).$\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(2)≈$\n{{field-2}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186379435 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=2x+y+3z,\\, && y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=x-y+2z,\\, && z(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy$ and $Δz$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{4}?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |\n\nTherefore, $y\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈$\n{{field-3}}\nand $z\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈$\n{{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186379478 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs above, where $t\\in R.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ The function $a(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1-t\\end{bmatrix}$ \n{{field-1}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $b(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix}$ \n{{field-2}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $c(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+1 \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix}$ \n{{field-3}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ {{field-4}} \nis a set of fundamental solutions to the system because the Wronskian \n\n$$\nW({{field-5}})={{field-6}}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n$\\,$ for at least one $t\\in R.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186379502 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=2x+2y-z,\\, && y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=x+y+3z,\\, && z(0)=0 \\\\ {w}^{′} &=wy+2xz,\\, && w(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  | {{field-3}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-4}},\n$z(1)≈$\n{{field-5}},\nand $w(1)≈$\n{{field-6}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186379515 "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=2x+z-w,\\, && y(0)=0 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=xz+y,\\, && z(0)=1 \\\\ {w}^{′} &=y-z+{w}^{2},\\, && w(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --