-3z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186400639 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 3x+7y &=1 \\\\ -2x-4y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186400646 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-3y &=6 \\\\ -2x+y &=-3 \\\\ 4x-4y &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186400867 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186401391 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${y}^{2}+z=9$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩ &=\\lambda ⟨\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,1⟩ \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2} &=1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186401398 "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y-x=0$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨y,\\,