\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186424019 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}20 & 10 & a \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ c & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186424085 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x}, & -\\sqrt{e}<x<-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & -1\\le x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186424087 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{5}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5x}, & 1\\le x<e\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186424143 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}(x-2),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186424144 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186424145 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the 