 the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,400.$ If the statistic $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{400}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nfind approximate values of $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186441118 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=130$ from a population where $35%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,130.$ Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{130}{X}_{i}.$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186441119 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=180$ from a population where $48%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,180.$ Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{180}{X}_{i}.$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186441120 "A box contains $70$ marbles, of which $30%$ are red and the rest are green. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th marble in the box is red} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,70.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186441121 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=45$ from a population where $20%$ of the population