\\end{aligned}$"] [#edb/ref 17592186482598 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=9y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=9x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186482602 "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186482611 "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186482613 "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\frac{3}{8{x}^{4}},\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186482617 "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What are the modes of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{96}{595}({x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}-2), & -1\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484194 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ and the line \n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t \\\\ y &=t-3, \\\\ z &=t\\end{aligned}\\right.$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484200 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4,\\, & 2\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484201 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-2t \\\\ y &=5-3t \\\\ z &=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x-2y+6z=62.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484204 "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 10 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{13}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186484211 "Find\n$|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 202 & 203 & 205 \\\\ 202 & 203 & 204\\end{aligned}|.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484213 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0.5 \\\\ 3 & -3 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484236 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere $(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+{z}^{2}=36$ and the line \n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t+1 \\\\ y &=2t+2, \\\\ z &=t+6\\end{aligned}\\right.$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484240 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1.9,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}, & 1\\le x<5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484244 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{12}=1$ and the line \n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3t \\\\ y &=2t, \\\\ z &=-2t\\end{aligned}\\right.$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484245 "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}$ equal to zero.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186484253 "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{30}$ be a random sample of size $n=30$ from a population with probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{15}x, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.66,$ calculate $P(2<\\overset{―}{X}<2.3).$\n\n*Hint: Two tables of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-1.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0606\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0594\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0582\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-1.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0735\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0721\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0708\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-1.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0885\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0869\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0853\\,$ <