f 17592186484276 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{2},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4{x}^{3}},\\, & 1<x<3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484278 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484286 "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ a & b-1\\end{aligned}|=5$,\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ a+2 & b\\end{aligned}|.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186484298 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=4$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{27}, & 0<x<3, \\\\ \\frac{9-x}{27}, & 3\\le x<9, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186485510 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $w$ and $v$ are vectors such that $x+w=v+x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $w=v.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\be