y+{z}^{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186495074 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t)+7 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [#edb/ref 17592186495114 "Find a Cartesian equation of the osculating plane for the curve $r(t)$ at the point where $t=1,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =-6t\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j+{t}^{3}\\,k \\\\ T(t) & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}(-2\\,i+2t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k) \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}[2t\\,i+(2-{t}^{2})\\,j+2t\\,k].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186495121 "![](images/49/495f9509b35049e62f7f67f8fac64378f5abf77fcef19afe2694b6f774b57b8d.png)\n\nConsider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2x+1 \\\\ x+y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the diagram provided to determine the solution $(x,y)$ of this system.\n\nThe solution is\n$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186495131 "Find the shortest distance between the origin and the osculating plane f