rac{3}{x+3}, & x\\ne -3 \\\\ 2, & x=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nhas an  infinite discontinuity at $x=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186504616 "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504617 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6k-20{x}^{2}, & x\\ne 1, \\\\ -8, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$ \n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504620 "The function $h(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(x-c)^{2}+1, & x\\ne 2, \\\\ 2, & x=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$, what are the possible values of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504621 "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+k}-\\sqrt{k}}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 18, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, what is the value of $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504625 "Given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ has the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504628 "The function $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+k}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 2, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the value of $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504630 "The function $g(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2x+a}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 36, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504631 "Find all of the points where $f(x)$ below has an infinite discontinuity.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-x, & x\\le 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x-3}, & x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504635 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4y=2x.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ and ${y}_{2}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ \n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, we should seek a particular solution \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the following constraints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}{y}_{2}^{′} &=2x \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{y}_{1}+{u}_{2}^{′}{y}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that ${u}_{1}(x)=-\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ find the function $g.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504638 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3a-2ax, & x\\ne -2, \\\\ 14, & x=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2,$ what is the value of $a?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504646 "Find the $60$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504647 "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡3(x-k), & x\\ne 1, \\\\ 2, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504651 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x-2}, & x\\ne 4, \\\\ c, & x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4,$ what is the value of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504665 "Let be $f(x,y,z)$ a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(0,2,1)=8, & \\, & {f}_{x}(x,y,z)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y+z}}, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(x,y,z)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y+z}}, & \\, & {f}_{z}(x,y,z)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+y+z}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,2,1),$ estimate the value of $f(-0.01,1.98,1.05).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504667 "The function $f(x)$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1, & x\\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{x-1}, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nhas an  infinite discontinuity at $x=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186504674 "From **left to right**, the $x$-values  where the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5-x}, & x<5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-x}, & x\\ge 5,\\,x\\ne 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n has an infinite discontinuity are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,$ $x=$\n{{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186504676 "Find the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504677 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(a-x)^{2}-a, & x\\ne -3, \\\\ 9, & x=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3,$ **in ascending order**, what are the possible values of $a?$\n\n$a=$ \n{{field-1}}\nor\n$a=$ \n{{field-2}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504680 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=9$\n\nII. ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n\nIII. $A$ is indefinite"] [#edb/ref 17592186504699 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(c-x)^{2}+3c, & x\\ne -1, \\\\ -5, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$, what are the possible values of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504702 "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504708 "Find all of the points where $f(x)$ below has infinite discontinuities.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x+8}, & x\\ne -8 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}, & x=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504709 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4y=2x.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ and ${y}_{2}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ \n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, we should seek a particular solution \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the following constraints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}{y}_{2}^{′} &=2x \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{y}_{1}+{u}_{2}^{′}{y}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that ${u}_{2}(x)=\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ find the function $g.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505001 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - 8y - 31 &=0 \\\\ 2x - 4y - 6 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505002 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7a - 8b + 41 &=0 \\\\ 4a - 4b + 20 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505004 "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y &=-7 \\\\ 2x - 3y &=13\\end{aligned}\\right.$."] [#edb/ref 17592186505005 "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6p - 9q &=-6 \\\\ 3p + 3q &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505044 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6p - 4q + 68 &=0 \\\\ 4p + 4q + 12 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505050 "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x + 2y &=17 \\\\ 3x + 3y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505053 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6p + 4q + 14 &=0 \\\\ 2p + 4q + 6 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505059 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2q + 16 &=0 \\\\ 2p + 4q + 28 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505062 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3u - 10v - 24 &=0 \\\\ 2u + 4v - 8 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505067 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9x - 9y + 54 &=0 \\\\ 4x + 8y - 16 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505080 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x - 7y - 35 &=0 \\\\ 2x - 4y - 6 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505081 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4b + 32 &=0 \\\\ 5a + 2b - 19 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505084 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x - 10y + 7 &=0 \\\\ 4x + 8y - 16 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505739 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the third column of the matrix $P?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505754 "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $\\text{Im}(T)=\\{[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,y=z\\}$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$\n\nII. If $Tx=[1,-2,3]^{T}$ has no solution, then $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n\nIII. If $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\\}$, then $T$ is invertible"] [#edb/ref 17592186505766 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the second column of the matrix $P?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186505773 "The formula for the total number of people in a school is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P=NS+A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N$ is the number of classrooms, $S$ is the average number of students per class, and $A$ is the number of school administrators.\n\nFind an expression for $S$ in terms of the other quantities."] [#edb/ref 17592186506523 "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(5)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4,\\, & x\\le 5 \\\\ 5,\\, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186506524 "Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}$ given $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nLet $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ=A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t}={{field-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}=L\\{A(t)\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={A}^{′}(t)\\text{ }dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ $0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-5}}\\,\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n."] [#edb/ref 17592186506573 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)-8 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{2}(t)+9,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [#edb/ref 17592186506578 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [#edb/ref 17592186506597 "Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}$ given $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nLet $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ=A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t}={{field-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}=L\\{A(t)\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={{field-3}} \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ {{field-5}}, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-6}}\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186506601 "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(1)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+7,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 2x-3,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186507402 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{19}x\\sqrt{y}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,4\\le y\\le 9, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\ge 1.9).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186507413 "Find the value of the constant $b$ that makes the function $h(x)$ below continuous at $x=1.$\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{bx}, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186507417 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt{x}\\,y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<0.5).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186507427 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-b), & 2<x\\le 4 \\\\ 4-x, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nis continuous at  $x=4,$ find the value of $b.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186507439 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x-b}, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 4x-2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis continuous at $x=1,$ find the value of the constant $b.$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186507441 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186507443 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}\\,(x+{b}^{2}), & x\\le 3 \\\\ x-1, & x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nis continuous at  $x=3,$  find the possible values of $b.$\n\nArranged in **ascending ord