t probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}({y}^{2}+xy), & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186524005 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>1,\\,y<0.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186524007 "![](images/eb/eb5f10ce887ba9d167b2753618064fcdbf8d1f42371d733aacd56a8d8cb5e667.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(1,\\frac{1}{2}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186524016 "![](images/eb/eb5f10ce887ba9d167b2753618064fcdbf8d1f42371d733aacd56a8d8cb5e667.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186524024 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2}+y, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $y>1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186524025 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12}x{y}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\