(x)=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186580268 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-x},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580279 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(\\frac{1}{2}<X\\le 2).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580294 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{-|x/4|}}{8},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}h(x),\\, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2},\\, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186580305 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\ge 4).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580306 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{1-x/3},\\, & x\\ge 3 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186580307 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -6x-4y &=6,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system is consistent dependent\n\nIII. The system has no solution"] [#edb/ref 17592186580320 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}, & 0\\le x<2 \\\\ 1, & x\\ge 2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(1\\le X\\le 3).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580322 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\,x, & 1\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580880 "Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ calculate $P(X<3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x≈6.30168\n$$\n\n*The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580909 "Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ what is $P(X<3)$ expressed as an integral?\n\n*Hint: The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186580932 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t)-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }4]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*"] [#edb/ref 17592186580953 "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+3y.$ \nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1} &=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"] [#edb/ref 17592186580958 "Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ calculate $P(X<9).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{9}x{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x≈3.75560\n$$\n\n*The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186581655 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186581681 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{{x}^{6}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186581697 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{10(x-1)}{{x}^{6}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186581713 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{6},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{27}, & 0<x<3, \\\\ \\frac{9}{{x}^{4}}, & 3\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186581719 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈0.6931,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+4}{24}, & -4<x<2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 2\\le x<4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186581738 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12(x-1)}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186582343 "Suppose $n=8pq-4{q}^{8}+4,$ where $p,q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument.\n\nThe number $n$ is {{field-1}} since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =8pq-4{q}^{8}+4 \\\\  & =2({{field-2}}+2) \\\\  & ={{field-3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere  $a=${{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186582352 "Suppose $n=-8p+2q+7,$ where $p,q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument.\n\nThe number $n$ is {{field-1}} since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-8p+2q+7 \\\\  & =2(-4p+{{field-2}})+1 \\\\  & ={{field-3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=${{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186582354 "Suppose $n=10p-1,$ where $p\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is odd.\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =10p-1 \\\\  & =2({{field-1}})+1 \\\\  & ={{field-2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=$ {{field-3}}, which is an integer."] [#edb/ref 17592186582364 "Find the limit at $x=1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-1\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<1 \\\\ 2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=1 \\\\ 2-{x}^{2}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186582368 "Find the right-sided limit at $x=32$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 32 \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{x}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {32}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186582373 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+1 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}+2 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186582376 "Suppose $n=2k+2m-8km-4,$ where $k,m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument.\n\nThe number $n$ is {{field-1}} since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =2k+2m-8km-4 \\\\  & =2({{field-2}}-4km-2) \\\\  & ={{field-3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere  $a=${{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186582381 "Suppose $n=5-6k,$ where $k\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is odd.\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =5-6k \\\\  & =2({{field-1}})+1 \\\\  & ={{field-2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=$ {{field-3}}, which is an integer."] [#edb/ref 17592186582384 "Suppose $n=8k-4m+6,$ where $k,m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument.\n\nThe number $n$ is {{field-1}} since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =8k-4m+6 \\\\  & =2({{field-2}}+3) \\\\  & ={{field-3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=${{field-4}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186582386 "Suppose $n=12-10v,$ where $v\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even.\n\nThe number $n$ is even since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =12-10v \\\\  & =2({{field-1}}) \\\\  & ={{field-2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=$ {{field-3}}, which is an integer."] [#edb/ref 17592186582387 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{4})+3x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,-2<x\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{4})+kx\\, & \\text{ for }\\,1<x<4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ exists. What is the value of constant $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186582390 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the