y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186594674 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+x & \\text{ for }\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x<\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186594681 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$0\\cdot 0=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186594692 "$$\n∀{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}∣({x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}+3)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?"] [#edb/ref 17592186594700 "$$\n