imal places."] [#edb/ref 17592186601901 "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,y=2\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} &=f(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186601934 "For the initial value problem ${y}^{′}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =1,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\nI. The stability function is $R(Δx)=1-Δx+\\frac{1}{2}(Δx)^{2}.$\n\nII. The stability region is $|\\frac{1}{2}(Δx-1)^{2}|=1.$\n\nIII. The method is absolutely stable.\n\nIV. The method is stable for step size $Δx=1.5.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186602411 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}x, & 0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>3,\\,y>2.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186602433 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186603002 "Let $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2