ations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - y - 5 z &=6 \\\\ x + 2 y + 4 z &=-3 \\\\ - 2 x + 2 y + 10 z &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186610110 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2 x - 5 y + 11 z &=4 \\\\ - 2 x + 10 y - 16 z &=-4 \\\\ x - 5 y + 8 z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186610111 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 2 y + 2 z &=-2 \\\\ - 3 x - 6 y - 6 z &=6 \\\\ 2 x + 5 y + 6 z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186610124 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4 x - 11 y + 29 z &=-6 \\\\ x - 3 y + 8 z &=-2 \\\\ - 3 x + 9 y - 24 z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186610134 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 2 y - 6 z &=-11 \\\\ x + y - 4 z &=-7 \\\\ - 4 x - 8 y + 24 z &=44\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186610166 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+42y-60z &=48 \\\\ 8x-56y+80z &=-64 \\\\ 4x-28y+40z &=-32\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186610171 "Consider the following